// A lambda inside a lambda is checked for shadowing in the scope the OUTER
// one is written in, not only in the one it is lowered in: by the time the
// inner one is lowered the enclosing method is the outer lambda's, and the
// names of this scope are no longer visible to be shadowed. Without that
// check `v` here would mean the local on one line and a parameter on the
// next.
interface Get { int of(int a); }
interface Make { Get build(int k); }
int v = 1;
Make m = (int k) => (int v) => v + k;
print(m.build(2).of(3));
